Sun Oct 25 14:19:39 UTC 2026 - Tomáš Chvátal <tomas.chvatal@gmail.com>

- books: drop the Recommends on opensuse-manuals_en and
  opensuse-startup_en-pdf and the Suggests on opensuse-manuals_de,
  opensuse-manuals_hu, opensuse-manuals_ru, opensuse-startup_de-pdf
  and opensuse-startup_ru-pdf. The opensuse-manuals source no longer
  builds any binary into the Tumbleweed repo, so the lines were
  silently inert.
- books: drop the Suggests on gcc46-info (the GCC 4.6 info pages
  are long gone; gcc-info remains), kiwi-doc, nfs-doc, php-doc,
  python-doc, python-doc-pdf, python3-doc-pdf, texlive-doc and
  yast2-devel-doc. None of these names resolves to a binary, a
  Provides or an Obsoletes in the current repository; the kiwi
  documentation moved online and the texlive-doc meta package was
  removed (per-collection *-doc packages remain).
- books: rename apache2-doc to apache2-manual and selinux-doc to
  selinux-policy-doc. The documentation ships under the new names;
  the old ones survive only as compat Provides/Obsoletes.
- imaging: drop the Recommends on gimp-help and the Suggests on
  gimp-ufraw and ufraw. GIMP 3 no longer ships a help subpackage or
  the ufraw plugin, and ufraw itself is unmaintained upstream with
  its pattern role gone with the plugin.
- mobile: drop the Suggests on irda (IrDA support was removed from
  the distribution) and rename smbios-utils-python to
  python3-smbios-utils, the current package name.
- multimedia: drop the Suggests on vdr and xawtv; both packages
  were dropped from the distribution.
- technical_writing: drop the Recommends on docbook-xml-website
  and susedoc (both dropped from the distribution) and the Suggests
  on texlive-doc; rename mxml to libmxml1 and saxon to saxon10,
  the current package names; drop sablot, an XSLT processor dormant
  upstream for two decades whose role is covered by saxon10 and
  libxslt; remove the duplicated texlive-omega and texlive-xetex
  Suggests.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Oct 18 18:11:37 UTC 2026 - Tomáš Chvátal <tomas.chvatal@gmail.com>

- Stop pulling YaST into default Tumbleweed installations: drop
  the Recommends on yast2-sound from the multimedia pattern.
  Drop YaST from the pattern recommendations. The YaST patterns
  and packages stay in the repository for anyone who has them or
  wants them; new installations simply come without YaST.

